    howToRecognizeEn: 'Ticking digital clocks, flashing red text ("Almost gone!"), banners showing real-time visitor counts, and "limited-edition" flash sales.',
    whereEn: 'Hotel booking portals, airline reservation engines, e-commerce flash sales, and online course landing pages.',
    misconceptionsEn: 'Myth: "The website is legally required to tell the truth about stock levels." Fact: E-commerce platforms regularly deploy deceptive dark patterns that simulate scarcity with client-side JavaScript.',
    limitationsEn: 'Genuine physical scarcity exists (e.g. concert tickets in a 5,000-seat stadium, seasonal mango harvests); the distinction is whether the limit is physically real or algorithmically generated.',
    howToRespondEn: 'The Incognito Refresh Test: Open the product page in an incognito/private browser window. If the countdown timer resets back to its starting time or the "Only 2 left" count remains static, the urgency is completely fabricated.',
